        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Set up prep workflow, food safety checklist, and allergen reference.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M31",
            "speaker_id": 84871,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi all, I've drafted the prep schedule for the new menu items as part of T4. I've also created the first versions of A4 Prep, Cleaning, and Food Safety Checklist and A6 Allergen and Dietary Reference Sheet. Please review and let me know your thoughts.",
            "mentions": [
              9052,
              87779,
              150886,
              153726
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4",
              "A6",
              "T4",
              "T6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M32",
            "speaker_id": 153726,
            "reply_to": "M31",
            "text": "This is great, thanks. Looking at A6, for the yogurt dressing, where did we get the allergen info? Just want to be 100% sure we have it right.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M33",
            "speaker_id": 84871,
            "reply_to": "M32",
            "text": "Good question. I checked the labels on the yogurt and the tahini we use. It lists 'milk' and 'sesame' as allergens, which I've added to the sheet.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M34",
            "speaker_id": 150886,
            "reply_to": "M33",
            "text": "That's correct for the ingredients, but we also need to think about cross-contamination. The station where we mix dressings is also where we prep items with nuts for other dishes. To be safe, we should add a 'may contain nuts' warning to A6 for that dressing and add a specific cleaning step to A4 for that station before prep begins. This is a critical control point for T9.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6",
              "A4",
              "T9"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "warning",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M35",
            "speaker_id": 9052,
            "reply_to": "M31",
            "text": "The morning prep schedule looks really tight. Can we move some of the vegetable chopping for the salads to the afternoon before to save time?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M36",
            "speaker_id": 150886,
            "reply_to": "M35",
            "text": "We could for some things, but not for others. For example, the avocado for the chicken salad would oxidize and turn brown if we prepped it that far in advance. We need to keep that in the morning slot. However, we could definitely batch-cook the quinoa the day before. That would free up a lot of time and stove space.",
            "mentions": [
              9052
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 84871,
            "reply_to": "M34",
            "text": "Excellent point on the cross-contamination. I'll update A6 with the 'may contain nuts' warning and add the cleaning step to A4 immediately. Thanks for catching that.",
            "mentions": [
              150886
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6",
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thumbsup",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 84871,
            "reply_to": "M36",
            "text": "And batching the grains is a fantastic idea. That solves the morning rush issue. I'll adjust the prep schedule in T4 to reflect that. Let's lock that in as the final plan.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 87779,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "I've just cross-referenced the updated A6 against all the recipe cards in A2. With the new warning, all the information is now correct and consistent.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6",
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 84871,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "Perfect, thanks for double-checking. We can now consider the allergen information in A6 as validated and final.",
            "mentions": [
              87779
